b\n    - Show entity mentions in findings view\n    - Auto-suggest related perspectives\n\n21. **Source Traceability**\n    - Click finding → see supporting sources highlighted\n    - Click source → see findings it supports\n    - Bidirectional reference browser\n\n22. **Entity Context**\n    - When viewing entity, show all related findings/sources\n    - Display entity relationship graph\n    - Show mentions timeline\n\n23. **Gap Analysis Assistant**\n    - Suggest next research queries based on gaps\n    - Highlight data quality issues\n    - Recommend confidence improvement strategies\n\n#### G. **Customization & Workflow**\n\n24. **Layout Customization**\n    - User-preferred tab order/grouping\n    - Save custom filter presets\n    - Custom theme variants\n\n25. **Annotation Layer**\n    - Add notes/comments to findings\n    - Highlight important passages\n    - Share annotations with team\n\n26. **Smart Suggestions**\n    - \"You may also want to review...\" suggestions\n    - Contradiction resolution hints\n    - Gap filling recommendations\n\n27. **Batch Operations**\n    - Select multiple findings\n    - Bulk tag/flag operations\n    - Batch export\n\n#### H. **Integration & External**\n\n28. **API/Webhook Integration**\n    - Send report data to external systems\n    - Receive feedback on findings\n    - Integrate with documentation tools\n\n29. **Real-time Updates**\n    - If session is still being researched, live update findings\n    - Show new contradictions as they appear\n    - Current: Static snapshot\n\n30. **Version History**\n    - Track changes to report as it evolves\n    - Revert to previous states\n    - Diff between versions\n\n---\n\n### KEY CODE PATTERNS TO REFERENCE\n\n**File Locations:**\n- Shell: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\components\\report\\ReportShell.tsx`\n- View: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\components\\report\\ReportView.tsx`\n- Sidebar: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\components\\report\\ThemedSidebar.tsx`\n- Modal: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\components\\layout\\ReportModal.tsx`\n- Theme: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\components\\report\\core\\ThemeContext.tsx`\n- State: `C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\src\\stores\\appStore.ts`\n\n**Key Dependencies:**\n- Framer Motion: Animations and transitions\n- Zustand: State management\n- React Context: Theme provision\n- TypeScript: Type-safe data structures\n\n---\n\nThis Report Shell & Navigation system represents a well-architected modal report viewer with sophisticated theming, flexible filtering, and clear separation of concerns. The dual-theme implementation (Radar/Swiss) is particularly elegant, and the integration with Zustand state management keeps the component tree clean. Enhancement opportunities primarily focus on extending capabilities (exports, comparisons, visualizations) and improving workflows (keyboard shortcuts, persistence, batch operations)."}],"totalDurationMs":186737,"totalTokens":39241,"totalToolUseCount":16,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10497,"cache_read_input_tokens":28736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10497},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
[2026-01-29T23:35:39.128Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114WFKBqqHY41UxaeWCskU1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive analysis.\n\n## Comprehensive Analysis: Report Interactive Features System\n\n### 1. Current Functionality and UX Patterns\n\n#### **FocusMode Component**\n- **Purpose**: Full-screen modal overlay with spotlight effect that emphasizes content\n- **Functionality**:\n  - Modal overlay with darkened background and radial gradient spotlight\n  - Theme-aware styling (Radar: dark with cyan accent; Swiss: minimal light)\n  - Close on backdrop click or ESC key\n  - Children content centered and constrained to max-width-3xl\n  - \"Press ESC to exit\" hint in top-right\n  - Ambient glow effect for radar theme\n\n- **SpotlightText Sub-component**:\n  - Sentence-by-sentence hover interaction (opacity fading on sentences)\n  - Keyword highlighting with theme-aware colors\n  - Split sentences by punctuation boundaries\n  - Individual sentence hover state management\n\n#### **SpeedReader Component**\n- **Purpose**: RSVP (Rapid Serial Visual Presentation) reader for accelerated content consumption\n- **Functionality**:\n  - Full-screen modal with large word display\n  - Focal point detection (optimal eye-tracking at 35% left of word)\n  - Word progression at configurable WPM (100-600, step 50)\n  - Progress bar showing current position\n  - Keyboard controls: Space (play/pause), Arrow keys (skip ±5 words), ESC (close)\n  - Play/Pause/Reset buttons\n  - Visual focal point markers (top/bottom indicators)\n  - Auto-completion pause at end\n  - Theme-aware styling with appropriate visual hierarchy\n\n#### **IntelDashboard Component**\n- **Purpose**: At-a-glance metrics display for research intelligence\n- **Functionality**:\n  - 12-column grid layout with mixed span cards\n  - Primary confidence gauge (4-column, 2-row span) with animated progress ring\n  - Metric cards showing findings/sources with optional trend indicators\n  - Gauge cards for coverage/reliability/completeness (small animated progress rings)\n  - Alerts section with pulsing animation when alerts > 0\n  - Confidence-based status indicator (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW)\n  - Animated number transitions with spring physics\n  - Color-coded metrics (emerald/amber/rose/cyan/blue/purple)\n  - Staggered entrance animations (0.1-0.35s delays)\n\n#### **KeyPointsPanel Component**\n- **Purpose**: Categorized, filterable summary of key intelligence points\n- **Functionality**:\n  - Type-based filtering (All, Insight, Warning, Action, Fact)\n  - Type counts displayed dynamically\n  - Expandable point cards showing:\n    - Icon (emoji-based: 💡 🚨 🎯 📊)\n    - Point text\n    - Confidence percentage\n    - Source count\n    - Optional related findings (expanded state)\n  - Smooth expand/collapse animations\n  - Highlight state for external selection\n  - Visual type coding with theme-specific colors\n  - Scrollable container (max-height-96)\n\n---\n\n### 2. State Management Approach\n\n#### **Local Component State Pattern**\nAll features use React's `useState` hook for local state:\n\n| Component | State Variables | Management |\n|-----------|-----------------|-----------|\n| **FocusMode** | `enabled`, `onClose` (props) | Props-driven, modal visibility external |\n| **SpotlightText** | `hoveredSentence` | Local hover state, useCallback memoization |\n| **SpeedReader** | `currentIndex`, `isPlaying`, `wpm`, `intervalRef` | Interval-based progression, ref cleanup |\n| **IntelDashboard** | None (pure presentation) | Fully data-driven via props |\n| **KeyPointsPanel** | `filter`, `expanded` | Type filter + expanded point tracking |\n\n#### **Effects Management**\n- **SpeedReader**: Multiple `useEffect` hooks for:\n  - Interval management (play/pause)\n  - Keyboard event listening (space, arrows, ESC)\n  - Auto-reset when `isActive` prop changes\n  - Proper cleanup on unmount\n  - Dependency array: `[isPlaying, wpm, words.length, currentIndex, isActive, play, pause, onClose]`\n\n#### **Theme Context Integration**\nAll components consume theme via:\n```tsx\nconst { theme } = useReportTheme()  // 'radar' | 'swiss'\nconst styles = useThemeStyles()     // Pre-computed theme styles\n```\n\n**Theme Styles Object** (ThemeContext.tsx):\n- Radar: Dark ambient (`bg-slate-950`) with cyan accents, glow effects\n- Swiss: Clean minimal (`bg-stone-50`) with stone accents\n- Per-component overrides for text colors, backgrounds, borders, gradients\n\n#### **Animation Framework**\n- **Framer Motion** for all animations:\n  - Entrance animations: `opacity`, `scale`, `y` transitions\n  - Interactive animations: `animate` on state change\n  - Progress animations: smooth interpolation\n  - Staggered delays using `transition={{ delay }}`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Integration Points with the Report System\n\n#### **ReportView Architecture**\n```\nReportView (theme provider wrapper)\n├── ReportThemeProvider (context wrapper)\n│   └── ReportViewInner\n│       ├── ThemedSidebar (tab navigation)\n│       ├── ReportShell (modal container)\n│       └── Main content area\n│           ├── OverviewView (uses IntelDashboard, KeyPointsPanel)\n│           ├── FindingsView\n│           ├── SourcesView\n│           ├── PerspectivesView\n│           ├── AnalysisView\n│           └── EntitiesView\n```\n\n#### **Data Flow Integration**\n- **OverviewView** → Primary integration point:\n  - Passes computed stats to `IntelDashboard`:\n    - `confidence`: avg_confidence from findings\n    - `findings`: count with high-confidence filter\n    - `sources`: source count\n    - `coverage`: (sources / findings*2) * 100\n    - `reliability`: (high-confidence findings / total findings) * 100\n    - `completeness`: 100 - (gaps * 10)\n    - `alerts`: red flags + perspective warnings\n  \n  - Generates `KeyPointsPanel` data from:\n    - Perspective insights (type: 'insight')\n    - Perspective warnings (type: 'warning')\n    - Perspective recommendations (type: 'action')\n    - Top 5 findings (type: 'fact')\n    - Max 12 points total\n\n#### **Feature Trigger Points** (Current Gap)\n- **No explicit feature toggles identified** in analyzed files\n- FocusMode/SpeedReader appear to be **available but not yet triggered from UI**\n- Likely triggered from:\n  - Toolbar buttons (not found in ReportToolbar.tsx)\n  - Right-click context menus\n  - Keyboard shortcuts\n  - View-specific buttons\n\n#### **Session Data Type Integration**\nUses `SessionWithDetails` interface containing:\n```tsx\n{\n  findings: ResearchFinding[]          // With confidence_score, finding_type\n  sources: ResearchSource[]            // With credibility_score\n  perspectives: ResearchPerspective[]  // With key_insights, warnings, recommendations\n  contradictions: ResearchContradiction[]\n  gaps: ResearchGap[]                 // With priority, gap_type\n  causal_chains: CausalChain[]\n  entities: KnowledgeEntity[]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. User Experience Friction Points\n\n#### **A. Feature Discoverability Issues**\n1. **No visible UI triggers** for FocusMode and SpeedReader\n2. **Keyboard shortcuts not documented** in UI (only shown inside components)\n3. **Feature descriptions missing** - users won't know these features exist\n4. **No onboarding or hints** for first-time use\n\n#### **B. State Isolation Problems**\n1. **No cross-feature state sharing** - each feature independently manages state\n2. **No feature state persistence** - WPM preference lost on feature close\n3. **No feature state indicators** - parent doesn't know feature is active\n4. **Conflicting modal layers** - FocusMode and SpeedReader both use `z-50`\n\n#### **C. Keyboard Conflict Risk**\n1. **Space key in SpeedReader** conflicts with:\n   - Search input focus\n   - Any form interaction\n   - Browser default scrolling\n2. **ESC key handling** - multiple listeners could conflict with report-level ESC\n3. **Arrow keys** - may conflict with scroll/focus navigation\n\n#### **D. Content Access Friction**\n1. **SpeedReader requires specific text content** - only works if text is pre-selected\n2. **No content auto-selection** mechanism\n3. **FocusMode children must be pre-rendered** - no dynamic content loading\n4. **KeyPointsPanel scrolling UX** - max-height-96 with overflow-y-auto may cut items abruptly\n\n#### **E. Theme Compliance Issues**\n1. **RadioButtons/inputs lack theme styling** - plain HTML inputs in styled components\n2. **Inline styles override theme** - hardcoded colors in some places (e.g., `color={colorMap[color]}`)\n3. **Input type=\"range\" not styled** - default browser range input visible\n\n#### **F. Mobile/Responsive Issues**\n1. **SpeedReader full-screen** - unusable on mobile screens\n2. **IntelDashboard grid-cols-12** - may not adapt well to small screens\n3. **KeyPointsPanel max-width constraints** - may be too narrow on mobile\n4. **FocusMode max-h-[80vh]** - limited space on small screens\n\n#### **G. Accessibility Concerns**\n1. **No ARIA labels** for dashboard metrics and panels\n2. **Emoji-based type icons** - not meaningful for screen readers\n3. **Color-only status indication** - no text fallback for colorblind users\n4. **Keyboard-only navigation missing** for KeyPointsPanel (no Tab support shown)\n5. **Hover states only** - SpotlightText requires mouse interaction\n\n---\n\n### 5. Opportunities for Enhancement\n\n#### **A. Feature Visibility & Discoverability**\n1. **Add feature toolbar** with visible buttons:\n   - Focus mode trigger\n   - Speed reader trigger\n   - Dashboard export\n   - Settings icon for feature config\n   \n2. **Create feature quick-access panel** with:\n   - Description cards\n   - Demo previews\n   - Keyboard shortcut hints\n   - \"Learn more\" links\n\n3. **Add contextual help overlays**:\n   - First-time user tutorial\n   - Tooltip on feature buttons\n   - Feature comparison guide\n\n#### **B. State Management Enhancement**\n1. **Lift state to ReportView level**:\n   ```tsx\n   const [activeFeature, setActiveFeature] = useState<'focus' | 'speed' | null>(null)\n   const [featureConfig, setFeatureConfig] = useState({ wpm: 300, highlightKeywords: [] })\n   ```\n\n2. **Add feature persistence**:\n   - LocalStorage for user preferences (WPM, theme choice)\n   - Zustand/Redux store for cross-session state\n   - UserPreferences table in backend\n\n3. **Create feature state context**:\n   ```tsx\n   <FeatureContext.Provider value={{ activeFeature, featureConfig, setActiveFeature }}>\n   ```\n\n#### **C. Content Integration Improvements**\n1. **Auto-detect content for features**:\n   - Selection-triggered SpeedReader\n   - Paragraph-level Focus mode\n   - Smart content extraction for dashboard\n\n2. **Add content source mapping**:\n   - Link IntelDashboard to findings/sources\n   - Click-through from KeyPointsPanel to full finding\n   - Breadcrumb navigation in Focus mode\n\n3. **Implement smart highlighting**:\n   - Extract keywords from perspective\n   - Auto-populate SpotlightText keywords\n   - Context-aware highlighting suggestions\n\n#### **D. UX/Interaction Improvements**\n1. **Implement feature stacking**:\n   - Allow Focus mode + SpeedReader together\n   - Support reading in focus mode at speed\n   - Nested modal support\n\n2. **Add gesture support**:\n   - Swipe to next/previous in SpeedReader (mobile)\n   - Long-press for context menu\n   - Pinch to zoom in Focus mode\n\n3. **Create smooth transitions**:\n   - Activate features without full modal (side drawer)\n   - Transition between features seamlessly\n   - Preview mode before full activation\n\n#### **E. Accessibility Enhancements**\n1. **Add comprehensive ARIA support**:\n   - `role=\"status\"` for animated numbers\n   - `aria-live=\"polite\"` for metric updates\n   - `aria-label` for icon-only buttons\n   - Accessible name for filter buttons\n\n2. **Keyboard navigation improvements**:\n   - Arrow keys to navigate KeyPointsPanel\n   - Tab/Shift+Tab for filter buttons\n   - Enter to expand/collapse items\n   - Configurable keyboard shortcuts\n\n3. **Visual accessibility**:\n   - High contrast mode toggle\n   - Pattern-based type coding (not just color)\n   - Larger font size option\n   - Reduced motion support\n\n#### **F. Performance Optimizations**\n1. **Memoization improvements**:\n   - Wrap IntelDashboard in React.memo\n   - Memoize metric calculations\n   - Cache computed keypoints list\n\n2. **Lazy load features**:\n   - Code-split features into separate chunks\n   - Load on-demand when feature activated\n   - Progressive enhancement approach\n\n3. **Optimize animations**:\n   - Use `will-change` CSS for animated elements\n   - GPU acceleration hints\n   - Reduce animation complexity on low-end devices\n\n#### **G. Advanced Features**\n1. **Annotation system**:\n   - Highlight text in Focus mode\n   - Add notes to KeyPoints\n   - Export annotations\n\n2. **Comparison mode**:\n   - Side-by-side finding comparison\n   - Contradictions view with focus mode\n   - Multi-panel synchronized scrolling\n\n3. **Smart summarization**:\n   - Generate key points automatically from text\n   - Extract main facts for SpeedReader\n   - Create focus-mode highlights from importance scores\n\n#### **H. Configuration & Customization**\n1. **Feature settings panel**:\n   - WPM range slider with presets\n   - Highlight keyword management\n   - Animation speed control\n   - Theme-specific overrides\n\n2. **Export capabilities**:\n   - Export KeyPoints as markdown/JSON\n   - Generate summary document\n   - Create presentation slides from dashboard\n\n3. **Integration hooks**:\n   - Webhooks for feature state changes\n   - Custom keyboard shortcut binding\n   - Plugin architecture for new features\n\n---\n\n### 6. Summary Table: Feature Capabilities vs. Integration Readiness\n\n| Feature | Maturity | Integration | State Mgmt | Accessibility | Mobile Ready |\n|---------|----------|-------------|-----------|----------------|--------------|\n| **FocusMode** | Complete | No triggers | Prop-driven | No ARIA | Poor |\n| **SpeedReader** | Complete | No triggers | Complex state | Minimal | Poor |\n| **IntelDashboard** | Complete | Well-integrated | None (pure) | No alt text | Fair |\n| **KeyPointsPanel** | Complete | Well-integrated | Local filter/expand | No keyboard nav | Fair |\n| **SpotlightText** | Complete | Not used | Basic hover | No SR support | Good |\n\n---\n\n### 7. Critical Integration Gaps\n\n1. **No master feature controller** - features are isolated components\n2. **No keyboard shortcut registry** - competing listeners, no customization\n3. **No feature state persistence** - preferences lost on close\n4. **No content binding** - features operate on generic children, no smart content selection\n5. **No mobile support strategy** - all features desktop-only\n6. **No analytics** - no tracking of feature usage for optimization\n\nThis represents a **foundational but incomplete** interactive feature system with excellent component architecture but missing the orchestration layer needed for production UX."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac11921 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"58218965-1ae9-4a11-8552-cd28b55cbac9","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read and analyze these files to understand the Report Interactive Features system:\n- src/components/report/features/FocusMode.tsx\n- src/components/report/features/SpeedReader.tsx\n- src/components/report/features/IntelDashboard.tsx\n- src/components/report/features/KeyPointsPanel.tsx\n- src/components/report/features/index.tsx\n\nProvide a comprehensive analysis of:\n1. Current functionality and UX patterns\n2. State management approach\n3. Integration points with the report system\n4. User experience friction points\n5. Opportunities for enhancement","agentId":"ac11921","con