hip data\n   - Missing contradiction, causality, or corroboration patterns\n\n#### Interaction Gaps\n1. **SwissView**:\n   - No search/filter capability\n   - No sorting options (by date, findings, sources)\n   - No session preview without opening report\n   - No comparison mode (multiple sessions side-by-side)\n   - No bulk operations\n\n2. **RadarView**:\n   - No legend displayed\n   - No color-blind friendly mode\n   - Single-level deep topic inspection (can't see sub-topics)\n   - No export capability\n   - Panel for focused topic only shows session list, not aggregated stats\n\n#### Navigation Gaps\n1. **Cross-view Switching**: No easy way to view same data in alternate perspective\n   - Currently both views are separate entry points\n   - No synchronized state between views\n\n2. **Breadcrumb Navigation**:\n   - RadarView lacks breadcrumb (only implicit through focus state)\n   - No ability to jump directly to specific levels\n\n3. **Session Context**:\n   - Clicking a session opens modal (external UI)\n   - No inline preview or detailed view within visualization\n\n#### Performance/Scalability Gaps\n1. **Large Dataset Handling**:\n   - RadarView canvas rendering might struggle with 100+ templates\n   - No pagination or virtualization in SwissView table\n   - No lazy loading of topics\n\n2. **Animation Overhead**:\n   - RadarView continuous requestAnimationFrame even when unfocused\n   - Constant hover detection in large node lists (O(n) per move)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Opportunities for Enhancement\n\n#### A. Enhanced Data Representation\n1. **Nested Visualization**:\n   - SwissView: Add mini-charts to template cards (pie chart of finding types)\n   - RadarView: Use concentric circles for finding type breakdown per session\n\n2. **Temporal Dimension**:\n   - Color gradient by recency (newer = brighter)\n   - Timeline slider to filter by date range\n   - Animated playback showing research evolution\n\n3. **Quality Metrics**:\n   - Node size/brightness by average confidence score\n   - Border style indicating verification status\n   - Glow intensity by source diversity\n\n4. **Relationship Network**:\n   - Optional overlay showing contradictions (red threads)\n   - Causality chains (green paths)\n   - Corroboration strength (thickness of connection)\n\n#### B. Advanced Interactions\n1. **Multi-Select & Operations**:\n   - Checkbox selection of sessions\n   - Bulk export/compare\n   - Create combined report from multiple sessions\n\n2. **Advanced Filtering**:\n   - Filter by finding type, source type, confidence range\n   - Date range picker\n   - Search across titles and queries\n   - Topic hierarchy navigation (collapse/expand)\n\n3. **Drill-Down Intelligence**:\n   - Click finding type to see its breakdown\n   - Click source to see credibility details\n   - Click confidence range to see distribution\n\n4. **Comparison Mode**:\n   - Side-by-side session comparison\n   - Template comparison (e.g., financial vs. competitive analyses of same entity)\n   - Finding type distribution across templates\n\n#### C. Hybrid Visualization Opportunities\n1. **Timeline View**:\n   - Horizontal timeline with session events\n   - Vertical slots for templates\n   - Finding dates shown as markers\n\n2. **Sankey/Flow Diagram**:\n   - Show flow from sources → findings → perspectives\n   - Weighted by frequency/importance\n\n3. **Matrix View**:\n   - Rows = templates, columns = topics\n   - Cell color/size = session count or finding count\n   - Hover to see details\n\n4. **Geo-Spatial View**:\n   - If sessions have location data\n   - Map-based distribution of findings\n   - Regional analysis clustering\n\n#### D. Smart UX Features\n1. **Responsive Visualization**:\n   - Adapt between SwissView (large) and RadarView (medium) automatically\n   - Mobile-friendly card-based list view for small screens\n\n2. **Smart Defaults**:\n   - Highlight templates with recent activity\n   - Suggest focus based on session count or finding quality\n   - Auto-expand topics with high contradiction rates\n\n3. **Contextual Help**:\n   - Tooltips explaining template types\n   - Guidance on finding type meanings\n   - Legend that's always accessible\n\n4. **Export & Sharing**:\n   - Generate visualization snapshots\n   - Export filtered view as SVG/PNG\n   - Share focused state via URL parameters\n\n#### E. Analytics Layer\n1. **Statistics Dashboard**:\n   - Trend analysis (findings over time)\n   - Template comparison metrics\n   - Finding type distribution across workspace\n   - Source credibility breakdown\n\n2. **Insights Generation**:\n   - Flag unusual patterns (anomalies)\n   - Suggest connections between topics\n   - Recommend next research directions\n\n3. **Quality Metrics**:\n   - Coverage analysis (which areas under-researched)\n   - Corroboration strength visualization\n   - Contradiction highlights\n\n---\n\n### 6. Technical Implementation Insights\n\n#### SwissView Architecture\n- **State Management**: 4-level navigation via `NavigationState` object\n- **Memoization**: Extensive use of `useMemo` for grouping and filtering (good)\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with semantic sizing (col-span-4/6/12)\n- **Rendering**: No virtualization (all sessions render in table)\n\n#### RadarView Architecture\n- **Canvas Rendering**: Custom 2D canvas with requestAnimationFrame loop\n- **Physics**: Circular orbit positioning, pulsing sine wave animation\n- **Hit Detection**: Simple distance-based (O(n) per mouse move)\n- **State**: Three independent axes (view, hoveredNode, focusedTemplate)\n- **Effects**: Cleanup on unmount; redraw on view/session/focus changes\n\n#### Data Flow\n1. Component mounts → `fetchTopics()` \n2. Sessions come from parent props\n3. Store updates propagate via state changes\n4. `useMemo` dependencies trigger recalculations\n5. Session selection via callback prop\n\n#### Color/Template System\n- Centralized in `appStore.ts` with lookup functions\n- Consistent across both visualizations\n- 10 templates with unique colors and display names\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table: Feature Comparison\n\n| Feature | SwissView | RadarView |\n|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| Navigation Type | Hierarchical | Spatial/Graph |\n| Max Visible Items | ~50 (treemap) | ~30 (canvas) |\n| Focus Mechanics | Level-based | Template-based |\n| Interaction Primary | Click/Select | Drag/Zoom/Click |\n| Animation | Static | Continuous |\n| Suitable For | Large dataset overview | Pattern discovery |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard nav possible | Canvas-based (harder) |\n| Mobile-Friendly | Better (grid-based) | Worse (needs drag/zoom) |\n| Information Density | High (text-heavy) | Medium (visual-heavy) |\n\n---\n\nThis analysis reveals a sophisticated dual-paradigm visualization system designed for research session management, with clear strengths in progressive disclosure (Swiss) and spatial exploration (Radar), but with significant opportunity for enrichment through temporal, relationship, and quality-metric visualizations."}],"totalDurationMs":71576,"totalTokens":37670,"totalToolUseCount":5,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10396,"cache_read_input_tokens":27266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10396},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
[2026-01-29T23:37:02.067Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FnERf2c5e8JwRHerX7DxK2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→'use client';\n     2→\n     3→import { useState, useEffect, useCallback, useRef } from 'react';\n     4→\n     5→interface VideoConfig {\n     6→  fps: number;\n     7→  durationInFrames: number;\n     8→}\n     9→\n    10→interface PlaybackState {\n    11→  frame: number;\n    12→  playing: boolean;\n    13→  progress: number;\n    14→}\n    15→\n    16→export function useVideoPlayback(config: VideoConfig) {\n    17→  const { fps, durationInFrames } = config;\n    18→  const [state, setState] = useState<PlaybackState>({ frame: 0, playing: false, progress: 0 });\n    19→  const frameRef = useRef(0);\n    20→  const lastTimeRef = useRef(0);\n    21→\n    22→  const play = useCallback(() => setState(s => ({ ...s, playing: true })), []);\n    23→  const pause = useCallback(() => setState(s => ({ ...s, playing: false })), []);\n    24→  const toggle = useCallback(() => setState(s => ({ ...s, playing: !s.playing })), []);\n    25→  const reset = useCallback(() => {\n    26→    frameRef.current = 0;\n    27→    setState({ frame: 0, playing: false, progress: 0 });\n    28→  }, []);\n    29→  const seekTo = useCallback((frame: number) => {\n    30→    const clamped = Math.max(0, Math.min(durationInFrames - 1, frame));\n    31→    frameRef.current = clamped;\n    32→    setState(s => ({ ...s, frame: clamped, progress: clamped / (durationInFrames - 1) }));\n    33→  }, [durationInFrames]);\n    34→\n    35→  useEffect(() => {\n    36→    if (!state.playing) return;\n    37→\n    38→    const frameDuration = 1000 / fps;\n    39→    let animationId: number;\n    40→\n    41→    const tick = (time: number) => {\n    42→      if (!lastTimeRef.current) lastTimeRef.current = time;\n    43→      const delta = time - lastTimeRef.current;\n    44→\n    45→      if (delta >= frameDuration) {\n    46→        const framesToAdd = Math.floor(delta / frameDuration);\n    47→        frameRef.current = Math.min(frameRef.current + framesToAdd, durationInFrames - 1);\n    48→        lastTimeRef.current = time - (delta % frameDuration);\n    49→\n    50→        setState(s => ({\n    51→          ...s,\n    52→          frame: frameRef.current,\n    53→          progress: frameRef.current / (durationInFrames - 1),\n    54→        }));\n    55→\n    56→        if (frameRef.current >= durationInFrames - 1) {\n    57→          setState(s => ({ ...s, playing: false }));\n    58→          return;\n    59→        }\n    60→      }\n    61→\n    62→      animationId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    63→    };\n    64→\n    65→    lastTimeRef.current = 0;\n    66→    animationId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    67→\n    68→    return () => cancelAnimationFrame(animationId);\n    69→  }, [state.playing, fps, durationInFrames]);\n    70→\n    71→  return { ...state, play, pause, toggle, reset, seekTo, config };\n    72→}\n    73→\n    74→// Smooth easing functions\n    75→export function easeOutCubic(t: number): number {\n    76→  return 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 3);\n    77→}\n    78→\n    79→export function easeOutQuart(t: number): number {\n    80→  return 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 4);\n    81→}\n    82→\n    83→export function easeInOutCubic(t: number): number {\n    84→  return t < 0.5 ? 4 * t * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 3) / 2;\n    85→}\n    86→\n    87→export function easeOutExpo(t: number): number {\n    88→  return t === 1 ? 1 : 1 - Math.pow(2, -10 * t);\n    89→}\n    90→\n    91→// Interpolation with smooth easing\n    92→export function interpolate(\n    93→  input: number,\n    94→  inputRange: [number, number],\n    95→  outputRange: [number, number],\n    96→  options?: {\n    97→    extrapolateLeft?: 'clamp' | 'extend';\n    98→    extrapolateRight?: 'clamp' | 'extend';\n    99→    easing?: (t: number) => number;\n   100→  }\n   101→): number {\n   102→  const [inMin, inMax] = inputRange;\n   103→  const [outMin, outMax] = outputRange;\n   104→  const { extrapolateLeft = 'extend', extrapolateRight = 'extend', easing } = options || {};\n   105→\n   106→  // Clamp input if needed\n   107→  let clampedInput = input;\n   108→  if (extrapolateLeft === 'clamp' && input < inMin) clampedInput = inMin;\n   109→  if (extrapolateRight === 'clamp' && input > inMax) clampedInput = inMax;\n   110→\n   111→  // Calculate normalized progress (0 to 1)\n   112→  let t = (clampedInput - inMin) / (inMax - inMin);\n   113→  t = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, t));\n   114→\n   115→  // Apply easing if provided\n   116→  if (easing) t = easing(t);\n   117→\n   118→  return outMin + t * (outMax - outMin);\n   119→}\n   120→\n   121→// Smooth spring with critically damped behavior (no overshoot, no jitter)\n   122→export function spring(params: {\n   123→  frame: number;\n   124→  fps: number;\n   125→  delay?: number;\n   126→  durationFrames?: number;\n   127→  easing?: (t: number) => number;\n   128→}): number {\n   129→  const { frame, fps, delay = 0, durationFrames = 20, easing = easeOutCubic } = params;\n   130→\n   131→  const adjustedFrame = frame - delay;\n   132→  if (adjustedFrame <= 0) return 0;\n   133→  if (adjustedFrame >= durationFrames) return 1;\n   134→\n   135→  const t = adjustedFrame / durationFrames;\n   136→  return easing(t);\n   137→}\n   138→\n   139→// Linear animation (for continuous motion like tickers)\n   140→export function linear(frame: number, durationFrames: number): number {\n   141→  return Math.min(1, frame / durationFrames);\n   142→}\n   143→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RXtY2QPAvhrW5Uxu