ality (Framer Motion + Gesture handling)\n   - Implement node dragging with physics (optional snap-to-grid)\n   - Add double-click to focus/zoom on subgraph\n   - Implement search highlighting (filter edges/nodes by keyword)\n   ```\n\n2. **Scalability & Performance**\n   ```\n   - Implement virtual rendering for 100+ node graphs\n   - Add edge bundling for large edge sets\n   - Optimize SVG with memo/useMemo for expensive calculations\n   - Add progressive force simulation (fewer iterations on resize)\n   - Implement quadtree for collision detection in NetworkGraph\n   ```\n\n3. **Relationship Metadata Visualization**\n   ```\n   - Add edge labels/badges showing relationship type\n   - Color-code edges by RelationshipType (not just 'contradicts')\n   - Add edge thickness based on strength/confidence\n   - Animate edge flow direction for causal relationships\n   - Show edge source count for multi-evidence claims\n   ```\n\n4. **Cross-Entity Relationships**\n   ```\n   - Extend EntityConstellation to show inter-type relationships\n   - Add connection type indicators (e.g., \"person→organization\" link)\n   - Implement relationship filtering UI\n   - Show relationship confidence/strength on edges\n   - Add temporal relationship indicators (before/after)\n   ```\n\n5. **Temporal/Contextual Awareness**\n   ```\n   - Add timeline slider coordinated with graph\n   - Highlight entities/relationships active in selected time period\n   - Animate graph evolution over time\n   - Show founding/dissolution events on entity constellation\n   - Link to CausalFlow for temporal chains\n   ```\n\n6. **Enhanced Accessibility**\n   ```\n   - Add keyboard navigation (Tab, Arrow keys, Enter for expansion)\n   - Pattern fills for nodes (striped, dotted) as colorblind indicator\n   - Semantic SVG with aria-labels and role attributes\n   - High contrast mode toggle\n   - Add node/edge descriptions in tooltip text\n   ```\n\n#### **Strategic Enhancements:**\n\n7. **Context-Aware Selection**\n   ```\n   - Synchronized selection across EntitiesView/SourcesView/NetworkGraph\n   - Breadcrumb showing selection path (Topic→Entity→Details)\n   - Highlight evidence chain when node selected\n   - Show related findings sidebar\n   - Cross-highlight sources supporting selected entity\n   ```\n\n8. **Layout Intelligence**\n   ```\n   - Adaptive force constants based on graph density\n   - Hierarchical layout option for causal chains\n   - Community detection for automatic clustering\n   - Sugiyama layout for DAGs (directed acyclic graphs)\n   - Circular arrangement optimized for edge crossings\n   ```\n\n9. **Rich Hover/Tooltip System**\n   ```\n   - Multi-line tooltips with key metrics:\n     * Confidence/Credibility scores\n     * Source counts\n     * Related entities count\n     * Last updated timestamp\n   - Tooltip positioning aware of boundaries\n   - Preview panel for entity details on hover\n   ```\n\n10. **Filtering & Search**\n    ```\n    - Filter nodes by type, confidence threshold, time period\n    - Search across all node labels with highlighting\n    - Boolean operators (AND, OR, NOT) for complex queries\n    - Save/restore filter presets\n    - Filter edge types separately from nodes\n    ```\n\n#### **Integration Opportunities:**\n\n11. **With Existing Components**\n    ```\n    - Link NetworkGraph edge clicks to ContradictionMatrix\n    - Connect EntityConstellation to EntityDetail panel\n    - Synchronize SourceNetwork selection with TrustRadar\n    - Timeline integration with CausalFlow\n    ```\n\n12. **Data-Driven Enhancements**\n    ```\n    - Show verification status with node appearance (glow, pattern)\n    - Encode entity roles via node shape (circle, diamond, square)\n    - Display claim corroboration count as node corona\n    - Show find confidence as opacity or halo intensity\n    ```\n\n13. **Export & Collaboration**\n    ```\n    - Export graph as SVG/PNG with legend\n    - Share graph snapshots with annotations\n    - Collaborative node annotations\n    - Generate graph summary/description\n    ```\n\n---\n\n### 6. ARCHITECTURAL INSIGHTS\n\n#### **Strengths:**\n- Clean component separation (3 specialized graph types + generic NetworkGraph)\n- Theme system properly abstracted (useReportTheme hook)\n- Framer Motion for smooth, professional animations\n- Type-safe interfaces for node/edge data\n- Responsive sizing based on container\n\n#### **Weaknesses:**\n- No reusable graph library (each component reimplements force/positioning)\n- Force simulation tightly coupled to NetworkGraph component\n- No shared edge rendering logic\n- Layout algorithms not parameterizable\n- No graph state management (useState scattered across components)\n\n#### **Recommended Architecture Refactor:**\n```\nsrc/components/report/visualizations/\n├── core/\n│   ├── useForceSimulation.ts (shared physics)\n│   ├── useGraphLayout.ts (layout strategy pattern)\n│   ├── GraphNode.tsx (reusable node component)\n│   ├── GraphEdge.tsx (reusable edge component)\n│   └── GraphInteraction.ts (shared hover/selection)\n├── layouts/\n│   ├── forceDirectedLayout.ts\n│   ├── concentricLayout.ts\n│   └── orbitalLayout.ts\n├── NetworkGraph.tsx (use shared components)\n├── SourceNetwork.tsx (use shared components)\n└── EntityConstellation.tsx (use shared components)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. CODE QUALITY OBSERVATIONS\n\n**Well-Implemented Patterns:**\n- Consistent use of React hooks (useMemo, useState, useEffect, useRef)\n- Proper dependency arrays preventing unnecessary recalculations\n- Clean prop interfaces with optional properties\n- Consistent animation transitions (spring damping values tuned well)\n- Theme-aware styling throughout\n\n**Areas for Improvement:**\n- Magic numbers in layout algorithms (50 iterations, 0.35 radius factor, etc.) should be constants\n- Force simulation parameters hardcoded (1000 for repulsion, 0.01 for attraction)\n- No error handling for missing data (assumes nodes/edges always exist)\n- No loading states or skeleton screens\n- SVG dimensions hardcoded (300x300 in SourceNetwork) should be responsive\n\n---\n\nThis analysis provides a comprehensive blueprint for understanding your current implementation and planning enhancements. The system is well-designed for its current scope but would benefit significantly from interactive controls, scalability improvements, and richer metadata visualization."}],"totalDurationMs":184729,"totalTokens":44551,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7408,"cache_read_input_tokens":37137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7408},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
