[2026-01-29T23:39:47.545Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01EpKvqaQDShSoxEpUuJaAUN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XyDaJrLanYVpiFyYYJ4mfS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/directions -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d \"{\\\"project_id\\\": \\\"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\\\", \\\"context_id\\\": \\\"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\\\", \\\"context_name\\\": \\\"Report Theming & Cards\\\", \\\"context_map_id\\\": \\\"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\\\", \\\"context_map_title\\\": \\\"Report Theming & Cards\\\", \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Implement comprehensive design token system with theme customization API and accessibility modes\\\", \\\"direction\\\": \\\"## Design Token System & Theme Customization\\\\n\\\\n### Vision\\\\nTransform the hardcoded dual-theme system into a flexible, extensible design token architecture that supports custom themes, accessibility modes (high-contrast, reduced-motion), and runtime theme customization - enabling white-label deployments and user personalization.\\\\n\\\\n### Business Value\\\\n- **White-label capability**: Customers can apply their brand colors without code changes\\\\n- **Accessibility compliance**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance with high-contrast and reduced-motion modes\\\\n- **User personalization**: Users can customize their experience, increasing engagement\\\\n- **Developer velocity**: Centralized tokens reduce inconsistency bugs and speed up new component development\\\\n- **Enterprise readiness**: Theme persistence and user preferences enable professional deployments\\\\n\\\\n### Scope\\\\n**Included:**\\\\n- Design token system with semantic naming (colors, spacing, typography, shadows, animations)\\\\n- Theme configuration API for runtime customization\\\\n- High-contrast accessibility theme variant\\\\n- Reduced-motion mode respecting prefers-reduced-motion\\\\n- Theme persistence via localStorage with user preferences\\\\n- Theme switching UI component with preview\\\\n- Migration of all existing components to token-based styling\\\\n\\\\n**Out of Scope:**\\\\n- Theme editor UI (future enhancement)\\\\n- Server-side theme storage\\\\n- CSS-in-JS migration\\\\n\\\\n### Key Components\\\\n1. **DesignTokens config** - Centralized token definitions for all visual properties\\\\n2. **ThemeProvider enhancement** - Extended context with full token access and customization API\\\\n3. **useThemeTokens hook** - Granular access to spacing, colors, animations\\\\n4. **AccessibilityProvider** - Manages reduced-motion and high-contrast preferences\\\\n5. **ThemeSwitcher component** - User-facing theme selection with live preview\\\\n6. **Token migration** - Update all 20+ themed components to use tokens\\\\n\\\\n### Technical Approach\\\\n- Define tokens as TypeScript constants with strong typing\\\\n- Use CSS custom properties for runtime theme switching\\\\n- Implement prefers-reduced-motion and prefers-color-scheme detection\\\\n- Store preferences in localStorage with fallback to system preferences\\\\n- Create component factory pattern for consistent themed component creation\\\\n\\\\n### Files to Create/Modify\\\\n- Create: `src/lib/design-tokens/tokens.ts`\\\\n- Create: `src/lib/design-tokens/themes.ts`\\\\n- Create: `src/lib/design-tokens/accessibility.ts`\\\\n- Create: `src/components/report/core/AccessibilityProvider.tsx`\\\\n- Create: `src/components/report/ThemeSwitcher.tsx`\\\\n- Modify: `src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx`\\\\n- Modify: `src/components/report/ThemedCards.tsx`\\\\n- Modify: `src/components/report/shared/*.tsx` (all shared components)\\\\n\\\\n### Success Criteria\\\\n- All color, spacing, and animation values sourced from tokens\\\\n- Theme can be switched at runtime without page reload\\\\n- High-contrast mode passes WCAG 2.1 AA contrast ratios\\\\n- Reduced-motion mode disables all non-essential animations\\\\n- User theme preference persists across sessions\\\\n- Custom theme can be applied via configuration object\\\\n\\\\n### Potential Challenges\\\\n- Migrating existing hardcoded Tailwind classes to token references\\\\n- Ensuring animation tokens work with Framer Motion\\\\n- Maintaining visual consistency during incremental migration\\\"}\"","description":"Save direction 1 for Report Theming context"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":155762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"fd600711-8bed-4cb2-b724-3623e3adffb5"}
