cted vs actual accuracy visualization\\n2. **BiasDetector** - Identify systematic over/under-confidence patterns\\n3. **PredictionTracker** - Log predictions and outcomes\\n4. **CalibrationComparator** - Personal vs population calibration\\n5. **BlindSpotIdentifier** - Areas of systematic error\\n6. **ImprovementRecommender** - Actionable calibration tips\\n7. **CalibrationTrend** - Historical calibration over time\\n8. **QualityScoreCard** - Aggregate research quality metric\\n9. **CalibrationExporter** - Export analysis report\\n\\n### Technical Approach\\n- Brier score for calibration measurement\\n- Statistical analysis for bias detection\\n- User-submitted outcome data for verification\\n- Rolling window for trend calculation\\n- Clustering for blind spot identification\\n- LLM for improvement recommendations\\n- Population data from anonymized aggregate\\n\\n### Files to Create/Modify\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/CalibrationDashboard.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/CalibrationChart.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/BiasDetector.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/PredictionTracker.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/BlindSpotIdentifier.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/calibration/ImprovementRecommender.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/lib/calibrationMetrics.ts`\\n- Create: `src/lib/biasAnalysis.ts`\\n- Create: `src/hooks/useCalibration.ts`\\n- Create: API route: `src/app/api/calibration/submit-outcome/route.ts`\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Calibration chart shows meaningful patterns\\n- Bias detection identifies real patterns\\n- Predictions can be tracked and resolved\\n- Personal vs population comparison is insightful\\n- Recommendations are actionable\\n- Trends show improvement over time\\n- Quality score correlates with research outcomes\\n\\n### Potential Challenges\\n- Collecting outcome data at scale\\n- Statistical significance with limited data\\n- Privacy in population comparisons\\n- Defining ground truth for subjective claims\"\n}\nEOF","description":"Save Trust Visualizations direction 3"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2202,"cache_read_input_tokens":154820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2202},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"5410b821-84e5-4303-8438-9e8713a3abe0"}
