eBundler** - Reduce visual clutter in dense graphs\\n6. **GraphMinimap** - Overview navigation panel\\n7. **NodeSearcher** - Find and highlight nodes\\n8. **GraphFilterPanel** - Filter by attributes\\n9. **GraphExporter** - Export visualization\\n\\n### Technical Approach\\n- Sigma.js or react-force-graph for WebGL rendering\\n- d3-force for physics simulation\\n- Louvain algorithm for community detection\\n- Dijkstra/A* for path finding\\n- Edge bundling via FDEB algorithm\\n- Canvas rendering fallback for older browsers\\n- Web Worker for layout computation\\n- Progressive rendering for large graphs\\n\\n### Files to Create/Modify\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/AdvancedNetworkGraph.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/HierarchicalClusterer.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/PathFinder.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/LayoutSwitcher.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/EdgeBundler.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/components/report/visualizations/network/GraphMinimap.tsx`\\n- Create: `src/lib/graphAlgorithms.ts`\\n- Create: `src/workers/graphLayout.worker.ts`\\n- Create: `src/hooks/useForceGraph.ts`\\n- Modify: NetworkGraph.tsx - Upgrade to new system\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- 500+ nodes render at 30+ fps\\n- Clusters form meaningful groups\\n- Path finding identifies relevant routes\\n- Layout algorithms produce clear visualizations\\n- Edge bundling reduces visual clutter\\n- Minimap accurately represents graph\\n- Search finds nodes instantly\\n- Export produces high-quality images\\n\\n### Potential Challenges\\n- WebGL compatibility on older devices\\n- Layout stability during interactions\\n- Path finding performance for large graphs\\n- Cluster label positioning\",\"summary\":\"Build advanced force-directed graph with hierarchical clustering, path finding, and dynamic layout algorithms\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"requirement_id\":nu