[2026-01-29T23:55:06.671Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YFeMxeEj5LMbyfCXBK2Mpm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WxoMSf6LEYdDafcC7oC1cc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/directions -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d @- << 'EOF'\n{\n  \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n  \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727807388_g0e6x6e\",\n  \"context_name\": \"Network & Relationship Graphs\",\n  \"context_map_id\": \"ctx_1769727807388_g0e6x6e\",\n  \"context_map_title\": \"Network & Relationship Graphs\",\n  \"summary\": \"Implement collaborative network annotation with shared markup, comments, and team investigation workflows\",\n  \"direction\": \"## Collaborative Network Annotation System\\n\\n### Vision\\nTransform network visualizations from read-only displays into collaborative investigation canvases where teams can annotate entities, mark suspicious connections, add notes, and build shared understanding of complex relationship networks - enabling team-based research investigations.\\n\\n### Business Value\\n- **Team collaboration**: Multiple investigators can work on the same network simultaneously\\n- **Institutional knowledge**: Annotations persist and accumulate team insights\\n- **Investigation workflows**: Support for marking entities as 'verified', 'suspicious', 'needs review'\\n- **Audit trail**: Track who identified what connections and when\\n- **Export evidence**: Generate annotated network reports for stakeholders\\n\\n### Scope\\n**Included:**\\n- Annotation layer overlay on all network visualizations\\n- Entity markup (colors, icons, flags) with custom labels\\n- Connection annotations (strength, confidence, notes)\\n- Comment threads attached to entities and connections\\n- Status workflow (unreviewed → investigating → verified/flagged)\\n- Real-time sync of annotations across team members\\n- Annotation search and filtering\\n- Export annotated networks as images/PDFs with legend\\n- Version history for annotations\\n\\n**Out of Scope:**\\n- Video chat or real-time cursor sharing\\n- AI-powered annotation suggestions (future enhancement)\\n- Mobile annotation interface\\n\\n### Key Components\\n\\n1. **AnnotationLayer** - SVG overlay for visual annotations\\n   - Drawing tools (highlight, circle, arrow, freehand)\\n   - Entity markers (pins, flags, status icons)\\n   - Connection decorators (thickness, color, labels)\\n\\n2. **CommentSystem** - Threaded discussions on network elements\\n   - Popover comment panels anchored to entities\\n   - @mention support for team members\\n   - Resolution tracking for comment threads\\n\\n3. **StatusWorkflow** - Investigation state machine\\n   - Entity status badges (unreviewed/investigating/verified/flagged)\\n   - Bulk status operations on selected entities\\n   - Filter network by investigation status\\n\\n4. **AnnotationSync** - Real-time collaboration\\n   - WebSocket sync for live updates\\n   - Optimistic UI with conflict resolution\\n   - Offline queue with sync on reconnect\\n\\n5. **AnnotationExporter** - Generate shareable outputs\\n   - PNG/SVG with annotation overlay\\n   - PDF report with entity list and notes\\n   - Structured data export (JSON)\\n\\n### Technical Approach\\n\\n```typescript\\ninterface NetworkAnnotation {\\n  id: string;\\n  targetType: 'entity' | 'connection' | 'region';\\n  targetId: string;\\n  annotationType: 'marker' | 'comment' | 'status' | 'drawing';\\n  content: MarkerContent | CommentContent | StatusContent | DrawingContent;\\n  author: { id: string; name: string; avatar?: string };\\n  createdAt: Date;\\n  updatedAt: Date;\\n  replies?: NetworkAnnotation[];\\n}\\n\\ninterface AnnotationLayerProps {\\n  annotations: NetworkAnnotation[];\\n  onAnnotate: (annotation: Omit<NetworkAnnotation, 'id' | 'createdAt'>) => void;\\n  selectedTool: 'select' | 'marker' | 'comment' | 'draw';\\n  currentUser: User;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- Use SVG overlay positioned absolutely over network canvas\\n- Implement annotation storage in Supabase with real-time subscriptions\\n- Use CRDT for conflict-free concurrent edits\\n- Leverage existing theme system for annotation colors\\n\\n### Files to Create/Modify\\n\\n**Create:**\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/annotations/AnnotationLayer.tsx`\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/annotations/AnnotationToolbar.tsx`\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/annotations/CommentPopover.tsx`\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/annotations/StatusBadge.tsx`\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/annotations/DrawingCanvas.tsx`\\n- `src/hooks/useNetworkAnnotations.ts`\\n- `src/lib/annotations/sync.ts`\\n- `src/lib/annotations/export.ts`\\n- `src/types/annotations.ts`\\n\\n**Modify:**\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/NetworkGraph.tsx` - Add annotation layer integration\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/EntityConstellation.tsx` - Add annotation support\\n- `src/components/report/visualizations/SourceNetwork.tsx` - Add annotation support\\n\\n### Success Criteria\\n- Team members can add annotations that sync in real-time\\n- Comments can be threaded and resolved\\n- Entities can be marked with investigation status\\n- Annotations persist across sessions\\n- Annotated networks can be exported as images/PDFs\\n- Annotation history shows who made what changes\\n\\n### Potential Challenges\\n- **SVG coordinate mapping**: Ensuring annotations stay anchored during zoom/pan\\n- **Conflict resolution**: Multiple users editing same annotation\\n- **Performance**: Large annotation sets with many comments\\n- **Mobile support**: Touch-friendly annotation controls\"\n}\nEOF","description":"Save direction 3 for Network & Relationship Graphs context"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23440,"cache_read_input_tokens":21525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23440},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"00ce273a-2f1f-4d5a-a1a1-b536f9f1b925"}
